pokeheartgold-widepointers2.patch (tools/pokehg_gen.py applies it to build/pokeheartgold, after widepointers): the
pointer casts clang still reports once widepointers is in. GENERATED, never edited by hand: on a working copy with the
earlier patches applied, `python3 tools/pokehg_cc.py`, then `python3 tools/pokehg_widen.py --casts build/pokehg_cc`, then
`git -C build/pokeheartgold diff -U2 -- '*.c' '*.h'` (against the earlier patches) below this header.
- every cast of a pointer to a 32-bit integer, an int typedef or an enum clang reports (-Wpointer-to-int-cast,
  -Wvoid-pointer-to-int-cast, -Wpointer-to-enum-cast) as an intptr_t / uintptr_t cast at the column clang gives, as
  pokeplatinum-widepointers.patch: 90 files with the rules below at the pin a53ce07bc (95d5f7f1d: 835). Never worse than before (a
  result stored in a u32 is cut as it was), right wherever the address is computed on and cast back; Ghidra's
  pointer-through-enum casts ((T *)((enum Move)(p))) no longer cut the pointer.
- the int a cast to a pointer reads, when the operand is a plain name (`(T *)(param_1 + 4)`, `(T *)base`; not `p[i]`, `p->f`,
  `f(x)`): a local becomes intptr_t / uintptr_t, a parameter too in its definition and every prototype of the
  function by position (the u8 and u16 ones are left). The address was cut to 32 bits where the
  int was filled from a pointer before; callers' pointers convert as before.
- a local such a cast starts (`u32 x = (u32)p + n`, `x = (u32)p`) is an intptr_t / uintptr_t, as
  pokeplatinum-widepointers2.patch.
- Not done: casts inside macros (poke_overlay.c's HW_DTCM bounds, trainer_ai.c's OFFSET_OF: an offset, harmless).

